pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  # ---------- header ----------
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 38, 700, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        PUTTING IT TOGETHER — ONTOLOGY · SEMANTIC LAYER · KPI STORE
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 58, 760, 44]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        One question, one governed path to the answer
  - elementId: title-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 118, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- the question ----------
  - elementId: question-band
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 134, 832, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: question-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [84, 134, 792, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 13.5
      color: "$ink"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p>The question: <strong>"What is unbilled exposure by payer this week?"</strong></p>

  # ---------- flow: four stages ----------
  # stage 1 — ontology
  - elementId: st1-box
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 196, 196, 110]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ontSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: st1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [78, 208, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$ont"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        1 · ONTOLOGY
  - elementId: st1-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [78, 224, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        what the words mean
  - elementId: st1-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [78, 242, 168, 54]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>"Payer" and "unbilled" each mean one thing, governed in o2c-meaning.ttl</p>
  - elementId: arr-1
    elementType: line
    bounds: [262, 250, 12, 2]
    viewBox: [12, 2]
    points: "0,1 12,1"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [null, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$faint"}
  # stage 2 — semantic layer
  - elementId: st2-box
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [276, 196, 196, 110]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$slSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$sl"}
  - elementId: st2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [290, 208, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$sl"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        2 · SEMANTIC LAYER
  - elementId: st2-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [290, 224, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        how to compute it
  - elementId: st2-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [290, 242, 168, 54]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Unbilled USD = Σ net gallons × contract price, over delivered tickets with no posted invoice</p>
  - elementId: arr-2
    elementType: line
    bounds: [474, 250, 12, 2]
    viewBox: [12, 2]
    points: "0,1 12,1"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [null, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$faint"}
  # stage 3 — compiler
  - elementId: st3-box
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [488, 196, 196, 110]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$white"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$muted"}
  - elementId: st3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [502, 208, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        3 · COMPILER
  - elementId: st3-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [502, 224, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        one path to SQL
  - elementId: st3-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [502, 242, 168, 54]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Every consumer's question compiles to the same SQL — no hand-written forks</p>
  - elementId: arr-3
    elementType: line
    bounds: [686, 250, 12, 2]
    viewBox: [12, 2]
    points: "0,1 12,1"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [null, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.5, color: "$faint"}
  # stage 4 — KPI store
  - elementId: st4-box
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [700, 196, 196, 110]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ink"}
  - elementId: st4-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [714, 208, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$white"
      bold: true
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        4 · KPI STORE
  - elementId: st4-sub
    elementType: text
    bounds: [714, 224, 168, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "#C9C2B8"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        the certified number
  - elementId: st4-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [714, 242, 168, 54]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$white"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>The certified, versioned value every dashboard, sheet, and agent reads</p>

  # ---------- captions under the flow ----------
  - elementId: data-caption
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 320, 832, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      wrap: false
      align: [center, middle]
      text: |
        Underneath it all: the warehouse tables — the data stays where it lives and is queried in place
  - elementId: gov-caption
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 340, 832, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$muted"
      italic: true
      wrap: false
      align: [center, middle]
      text: |
        Governance runs across all four stages — everything defined in code, reviewed, and versioned

  # ---------- two closing columns ----------
  - elementId: why-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 382, 400, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Why the question needs both
  - elementId: why-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 402, 400, 88]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.45
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>"Payer" is meaning — the ontology's word. "Unbilled USD" is logic — the semantic layer's formula. Structure without logic is a taxonomy exercise; logic without structure is metric sprawl.</p>
  - elementId: kpi-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [496, 382, 400, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        What the KPI store adds
  - elementId: kpi-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [496, 402, 400, 88]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.45
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>A governed home for the result: certification status, owner, version, freshness. Consumers read the certified value instead of running their own query — so a Report C can no longer drift from Reports A and B.</p>

  # ---------- footer ----------
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 514, 620, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Flow mirrors the EPM demo's KPI pattern: candidate register → catalog → semantic layer → compiler → certified snapshots
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [830, 514, 66, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        05 / 05
